 Attempts to run the garbage collector. Note that this is subject to the same rules as the Lua API's collect_garbage function: memory may or may not be freed, depending on dangling references or other things, so make sure you don't have tables or other stack-referencing items currently alive or referenced that you want to be collected.
 
 
+On Lua 5.4 and 5.5, ``change_gc_mode_incremental`` leaves zero parameters
+unchanged and interprets the step size as a base-2 logarithm. Lua 5.5 converts
+positive step sizes to bytes and clamps them to the native ``int`` range before
+Lua compresses them. Negative step sizes leave the Lua 5.5 parameter unchanged.
+
+``step_gc`` retains its kilobyte budget. On Lua 5.5, the budget must be
+nonnegative and its byte count must fit the linked Lua build's memory type.
+Zero requests a basic collector step; older negative-budget debt adjustments
+have no portable Lua 5.5 equivalent.
+
+On Lua 5.5, ``change_gc_mode_generational`` sets the minor multiplier and the
+minor-to-major transition multiplier. Zero leaves either unchanged. The second
+parameter is not equivalent to Lua 5.4's major multiplier. Both mode-changing
+functions return the previous mode; older Lua behavior is unchanged.
